      "created_at": "2019-07-22T06:33:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"BrianleWolfhunt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/ebca7d/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> BrianleWolfhunt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That probably means they will collect the mini packs into one package and sell it like that (If I’m understanding their words correctly) instead of having them separate. I don’t imagine they will simply leave out those decks.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>To me it sounded more like the plan was to incorporate them into the larger expansions (which will already be combinations of existing expansions).</p>\n<p>I hope they do take the chance to make some minor alterations to a couple of decks - most decks still hold up pretty well, but there are just a couple like Bunker or Spite that could just use a small tweak to make them a lot more fun…</p>",
